        <mxCell id="p4-flow_81" value="async" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;strokeWidth=2;strokeColor=#B85450;dashed=1;endArrow=block;fontSize=11;labelBackgroundColor=#FFFFFF;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p4-flow_78" target="p4-flow_79">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p4-flow_82" value="The asymmetry is the design&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Taking stock is a command: orders asks synchronously, at placement, and needs the answer before it can&lt;br&gt;accept the order at all. Giving stock back is an event: nobody is waiting, the order is already over&lt;br&gt;whichever way it ended, and it has to happen even if orders is not in a position to ask.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;order.nullified collapses three endings into one topic, so a consumer holding goods needs one rule&lt;br&gt;rather than a subscription per way an order can die." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=14;fillColor=#FFFFE0;strokeColor=#CCCC66;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=2;fontSize=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="80" y="1130" width="1180" height="120" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p4-flow_83" value="Idempotence and ownership&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;· The saga releases from this service&#39;s own ReservationView, not from the message — an order edited after&lt;br&gt;  approval no longer matches the lines on the event that ended it.&lt;br&gt;· Releasing a hold that is gone is a no-op; a nullification arriving twice finds nothing to do.&lt;br&gt;· ReleaseReason separates an echo of the order&#39;s own decision from news it must act on — without it,&lt;br&gt;  releasing stock for a cancelled order would bounce back and reject the order that caused it." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=14;fillColor=#FFFFE0;strokeColor=#CCCC66;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=2;fontSize=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1320" y="1130" width="1180" height="120" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p4-flow_84" value="Legend" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=#B3B3B3;dashed=0;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontStyle=1;fontSize=12;fontColor=#333333;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="80" y="900" width="250" height="250" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
